course: dictionary
lesson: 3646
title: Helpers in our town
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A firefighter is a person whose job is to put out fires and rescue people and animals. You can see two parts in the word: fire and fighter, someone who fights fires.
explain: Read the words around it to learn more. «Wildfires spread fast in dry, hot, windy weather, so firefighters cut gaps to remove fuel.» Fuel is what a fire burns, like dry plants. A gap stops the fire reaching more of it.
explain: The words around a word can also tell you what to do. «You should never hide under a bed or in a cupboard during a fire, because firefighters may not find you.» Firefighters want you to get out and stay out.
explain: «Many people in town are there to help you: postal workers, doctors and nurses, police officers and firefighters.» Here firefighters are one of the helpers in a community.
fact: A firefighter is a person whose job is to put out fires and rescue people and animals.
fact: Firefighters also help in car crashes, floods and other emergencies.
fact: Firefighters work from a fire station and ride in a fire engine, also called a fire truck.
fact: Emergency numbers: 911 in the USA and Canada, 999 in the UK and Ireland, 000 in Australia, and 111 in New Zealand.
fact: Firefighters teach fire safety and say «get out, stay out».
exercise: «Firefighters cut gaps to remove fuel.» What is fuel here? | A type of fire engine | A rescue ladder | *Something a fire burns, such as dry plants | The water used to put out a fire
exercise: «You should never hide under a bed during a fire, because firefighters may not find you.» What should you do instead? | Go back inside for your toys | Hide in a cupboard | Stay under the bed and wait | *Get out and stay out
exercise: Grace says firefighters only put out fires. What is the right answer? | They only drive fire engines | *They also help in car crashes, floods and other emergencies | They never leave the fire station | They only teach in schools
test: Which phrase means the building where firefighters work? | Fire hose | *Fire station | Fire blanket | Fire alarm
test: In Australia, which number do you call in a fire? | *000 | 911 | 999 | 111
exam: Which of these is the best meaning of firefighter? | Someone who lights bonfires for the town | *A person whose job is to put out fires and rescue people | A fire engine driver who never leaves the station | A person who sells smoke alarms
